  "title": "Kirby Problem 3.74",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $Y$ be a rational homology sphere and $f:Y\\to Y$ be a self-diffeomorphism of $Y$. Suppose $W$ is a 4-manifold with boundary $Y$ such that $f$ extends to a self-diffeomorphism of $W$.\n\n(a) What constraints are there on the intersection form of $W$?\n\n(b) Does there exist a pair $(Y,f)$ such that $Y$ bounds a homology ball but $f:Y\\to Y$ does not extend over any definite manifold of either sign?\n\n(c) Develop methods for constraining the intersection form of $W$ that apply to indefinite, non-spin $W$.",
